                <pb facs="0952" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79620 Boeing Airplane Co./25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-11T10:00:00-03:30"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1928—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Department’s telegram 2 of February 6, 6 p.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d671-f1"
                    /> Military aviation authorities here report this morning Captain O’Neill and
                    companion in Comet aeroplane crashed near Minas last night. Latest information
                    affirms injuries to both aviators slight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
